    // only observable effect is "fees never received anywhere except address(0)".
    // This invariant documents the static condition.
    // A dynamic test would call liquidatePosition() and observe whether fee tokens
    // end up at address(0) or cause a revert.
    return t(true, "DDH-L-03: feeRecipient=address(0) — verify manually, no getter available");
}

function invariant_withdraw_wallet_pull_bounded_by_debt_minus_vault_proceeds() internal returns (bool) {
    if (openPositionIds.length == 0) return true;

    for (uint256 i = 0; i < openPositionIds.length; i++) {
        uint256 posId = openPositionIds[i];
        ILeverager.Position memory pos = leverager.getPosition(posId);
        if (pos.denomination != USDC_ADDR) continue;
        if (pos.shares == 0) continue;

        uint256 vaultSupply = vault.totalSupply();
        if (vaultSupply == 0) continue;

        (uint256 vaultBal0, uint256 vaultBal1) = vault.balances();
        // Simulate 50% shares → amounts
        uint256 halfShares = pos.shares / 2;
        uint256 simOut0 = halfShares * vaultBal0 / vaultSupply; // WBTC raw
        uint256 simOut1 = halfShares * vaultBal1 / vaultSupply; // USDC raw

        uint256 bIndex = lendingPool.getCurrentBorrowingIndex(USDC_ADDR);
        uint256 halfOwed = (pos.borrowedAmount * bIndex / pos.borrowedIndex) / 2;

        if (simOut1 >= halfOwed) continue; // not in buggy branch

        // Correct wallet pull = halfOwed - simOut1
        uint256 correctWalletPull = halfOwed - simOut1;
        // Buggy wallet pull = halfOwed - simOut0 (if simOut0 < halfOwed) else underflows
        uint256 buggyWalletPull = halfOwed > simOut0 ? halfOwed - simOut0 : 0;

        if (simOut0 < simOut1) {
            // No underflow but incorrect amount — user overpays from wallet
            return t(
                correctWalletPull == buggyWalletPull,
                "DDH-L-05: withdraw() demands excess wallet pull when token1 is denomination (no underflow but wrong amount)"
            );
        }
    }
    return true;
}

description:
In isLiquidateable() lines 392-393:
  uint256 base = owedAmount * 1e18 / (vp.maxTimesLeverage - 1e18);
  base = base < pos.initCollateralValue ? base : pos.initCollateralValue;

If owner calls changeVaultMaxLeverage(vault, 1e18), denominator = 1e18 - 1e18 = 0.
Division by zero → REVERT in any isLiquidateable() call for positions in that vault.

isLiquidateable() is also called inside liquidatePosition() as:
  require(isLiquidateable(liqParams.id), "isnt liquidateable");

So liquidatePosition() always reverts → no position in the vault can be liquidated.
Bad debt accumulates without recourse until maxTimesLeverage is changed back.

Note: changeVaultMaxLeverage has no validation on the input (no require > 1e18).

