description:
isLiquidateable() line 408 divides by (vp.maxTimesLeverage - 1e18):
  uint256 base = owedAmount * 1e18 / (vp.maxTimesLeverage - 1e18);
If the owner calls changeVaultMaxLeverage(vault, 1e18) (setting 1x leverage, intending to disable leveraged positions), the denominator becomes 0 → division by zero → panic revert. If set below 1e18, Solidity 0.8 underflow panics. Since liquidatePosition() calls isLiquidateable() (via `require(isLiquidateable(...))`), AND the collectFees modifier runs before that, ALL liquidations for the affected vault become permanently impossible. Existing leveraged positions accumulate bad debt that can never be recovered.

